{% set local_problem %}
<p>Surface drainage solutions have their place, but for Hampton Cove homes with significant landscaping investments, they often create more problems than they solve. Above-ground extensions are unsightly, get damaged by mowers, and can trip people. Splash blocks move water only a few feet and still cause erosion.</p>

<p>Hampton Cove homeowners invest significantly in their landscaping — and water dumping from downspouts can undo that investment quickly. Mulch washes away. Erosion develops. Carefully designed beds become drainage problems.</p>

<p>Underground drains solve all of this. Water disappears into catch basins at each downspout and travels through buried pipes to a safe discharge point far from your home and landscaping. It's the drainage solution that matches Hampton Cove's standards.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Underground drains connect to your downspouts via catch basins that collect water and filter debris. From there, solid PVC pipe carries water through buried trenches to a discharge point — typically 20-50 feet or more from your foundation.</p>

<p>We assess your property's terrain, identify optimal discharge locations, and design a system that uses gravity effectively while minimizing disruption to existing landscaping and irrigation.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've installed underground drainage systems on upscale properties throughout Hampton Cove. We understand that quality and aesthetics matter here — both in the finished product and in how we work on your property.</p>

